# README.md is fully rewritten on this branch: upstream's Install section
# describes config.sh / setup.sh / start.sh, which this deployment does not use.
# Without this, every upstream edit to their README (nine so far) would land as a
# whole-file conflict, since no region of the two versions corresponds.
#
# `merge=ours` keeps this branch's version on merge and discards upstream's
# changes to that file. It is NOT a built-in driver — it requires a one-time
# setting in every clone:
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# Without that setting git falls back to a normal three-way merge, so a forgotten
# config shows up as the conflict you would have had anyway, never as a silently
# wrong result. docker/check-upstream-drift.sh verifies it is configured.
#
# Upstream's README is never lost — read it with `git show main:README.md`, and
# the drift check reports when it changes so you can decide whether anything is
# worth porting across.
#
# Deliberately limited to README.md. The patched source files (app.py, auth.py,
# the flows) must keep conflicting: those conflicts are how upstream changes to
# the code this branch modifies get seen.
README.md merge=ours
